  "_module": "paralogue_site_correction",
  "_asks": "On the AF2 receptor the pipeline ACTUALLY docks each paralogue into: how far is the box the pipeline draws from where crystallography says ligands bind on that protein?",
  "_why": "`apo-pose-regime-dock.json` showed the Pocket-5 transfer docks a median +16.05 A worse than this protocol's own ceiling, on 11 of 11 in-regime pairs, while the receptor's own cavity sits at +0.39 A. That transfer is the step that places every ANTI-TARGET box, so every selectivity margin in the program is a comparison whose paralogue arms it drew.",
  "_scope": "re-scores nothing, moves no ddG, overturns no verdict. Emits a corrected site and a measured displacement; consuming them is a separate, explicit step per artifact.",
  "_no_dock": "geometric only \u2014 no smina, no fpocket, no seed, deterministic given the deposits",
  "pipeline_box_edge_A": 24.0,
  "nr4a3_site_untouched": "NR4A3's own box is built directly on the NR4A3 structure, NOT by `map_pocket_to_paralogue`, so it is not what this corrects and nothing here re-derives it.",
